<title>USA: Wells-Gardner gets credit deal extension.</title>
<headline>Wells-Gardner gets credit deal extension.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wells-Gardner Electronics Corp said Monday Harris Trust and Savings Bank of Chicago extended its long-term banking agreement until January 1, 2000.</p>
<p>The agreement provides a $7 million line of credit, which the company said is &quot;ample for our current growth plans.&quot;</p>
<p>The deal extends the company's October 1995 agreement, Wells-Gardner said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
